# Request vs Worker Boundary

- Keep synchronous request handlers focused on API-time behavior.
- Keep heavy enrichment, long-running AI work, and background processing in worker/queue paths unless there is a clear reason not to.
- Do not casually move worker logic into request handlers.
- If request-time code depends on background work, make that boundary explicit in the service flow.
